# Graphite macOS Light app icons

{{ ansible_managed }}

These icons were selected from [macOSicons.com](https://macosicons.com/) for personal customization. Each icon remains the property of its creator and the underlying brands retain their trademarks. Preserve the credits below. Do not resell the icons or present this selection as your own artwork or an icon-library product. A creator's specific license, if provided, governs that icon.

[Site terms](https://macosicons.com/terms) · [API terms](https://macosicons.com/developers/terms)

The original macOS icon files are downloaded with pinned checksums. An install-time Python tool extracts their native 1024×1024 PNG images without resizing, recoloring or re-encoding them. The manifest at `fedora/roles/niri/vars/macos-icons.yml` records source and PNG checksums. This light app-icon theme inherits Papirus-Dark, Adwaita and hicolor for folders, status symbols and apps installed later. The shell itself stays dark.

All currently installed launcher apps have a selected icon. Semantic substitutes are deliberate: T3 Code uses Script Editor, btop uses Activity Monitor, Online Accounts uses an account/profile icon, and Volume Control uses Sound Control. App names and launch commands stay unchanged.

